=head1 DESCRIPTION

The dollar value of the anomaly.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> MaxImpact => Num

The maximum dollar value that's observed for an anomaly.


=head2 TotalActualSpend => Num

The cumulative dollar amount that was actually spent during the
anomaly.


=head2 TotalExpectedSpend => Num

The cumulative dollar amount that was expected to be spent during the
anomaly. It is calculated using advanced machine learning models to
determine the typical spending pattern based on historical data for a
customer.


=head2 TotalImpact => Num

The cumulative dollar difference between the total actual spend and
total expected spend. It is calculated as C<TotalActualSpend -
TotalExpectedSpend>.


=head2 TotalImpactPercentage => Num

The cumulative percentage difference between the total actual spend and
total expected spend. It is calculated as C<(TotalImpact /
TotalExpectedSpend) * 100>. When C<TotalExpectedSpend> is zero, this
field is omitted. Expected spend can be zero in situations such as when
you start to use a service for the first time.



